# What must not travel to the build daemon.
#
# The Dockerfiles copy the whole workspace, because cargo needs it to resolve a
# workspace member. Without this file that means `target/` as well — which on a
# developer machine is tens of gigabytes, takes minutes to transfer, and can
# fill the builder's disk before the build starts. Everything listed here is
# either rebuilt inside the image or irrelevant to it.

# Build output. Host-shaped, and useless in a Linux image even when it is not.
target/
**/target/

# The docs site. Not part of either binary.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
docs-site/

# Python: virtualenvs, caches, wheels.
.venv*/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
crates/sdk/felix-python/dist/

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local artifacts a build must never depend on — and credentials it must never
# bake in. The last three are perf-session state that can hold tokens.
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
perf-results/
scripts/perf/cloud/sessions/
scripts/perf/cloud/session.env

# Prose. Changing a README should not invalidate a build layer.
*.md
docs/
